info.description:
End-to-end requests for the `voice-ai-lead-qualifier` n8n workflow.

Covers: happy-path call trigger, DNC block, out-of-hours queue, hot/warm/cold post-call routing, and idempotency replay. Each request includes automated tests asserting the response shape and expected DB side-effects.

## Usage

1. Import this file in Postman.
2. Set environment variables:
   - `base_url`   — your n8n instance, e.g. `https://your-n8n.example.com`
   - `lead_path`  — `/webhook/new-lead`
   - `retell_path` — `/webhook/retell-post-call`
3. Run requests in order — they share `lead_id` and `call_id` patterns.

## Reset DB between runs

```sql
TRUNCATE leads, call_attempts, processed_calls, call_queue,
         call_costs, nurture_queue RESTART IDENTITY CASCADE;
-- Keep dnc_list seed entry
```

## Schemas asserted

```ts
// HTTP 200 — call initiated
{ status: 'ok', action: 'call_initiated', lead_id: string, call_attempt_id: string }

// HTTP 200 — DNC blocked
{ status: 'blocked', reason: 'phone_on_dnc' }

// HTTP 202 — out of hours
{ status: 'queued', reason: 'out_of_hours', scheduled_at: string, queue_id: string }

// HTTP 200 — already queued (duplicate lead)
{ status: 'already_queued' }

// HTTP 200 — post-call hot
{ status: 'ok', intent: 'hot', bant_score: number, next_action: 'schedule_meeting' }

// HTTP 200 — post-call warm
{ status: 'ok', intent: 'warm', next_action: 'nurture' }

// HTTP 200 — already processed (dup post-call)
{ status: 'already_processed' }
```

